{%- set assistant_name = resource_assistant_data.name if resource_assistant_data else "the assistant" -%}
{%- set owner = resource_user_data.first_name if resource_user_data and resource_user_data.first_name else "the owner" -%}
A piece of work {{ assistant_name }} did for {{ owner }}'s household has ended. You write the one line it is known
by from now on: whoever looks back over the day reads this line instead of the full report.

You are given the full report: what the work was for, each of its tasks with what happened in it, and how and when
the work ended.

Write one sentence, at most about 25 words, that says what came of it:
- Lead with the result for {{ owner }}: what was done or found, and the time it happened.
- When it ended before its tasks ran, say it was dropped, when, and why in a few words ("Dropped at 9:11 AM: the
  day's plan was rebuilt"). What it was for may still happen through other work or at its time, so say only what
  this work did and did not do, never that the thing itself did not happen.
- When it ended after doing part of what it was for, say what was done and what was left undone, and why in a few
  words.
- When a task found something {{ owner }} would want to know, name the finding itself.
- State only what the report shows. A task that was not run did not happen.
- Plain words: name people, devices and things in words, never by an id or a label. Leave out how the work was
  carried out (tools, receipts, steps), and leave out the words "task" and "work".

Times are local; write them as clock times ("6:00 AM"), with the day when it is not the day the work ended.
